course: dictionary
lesson: 15812
title: Unclaimed: nobody has come to collect it
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things are left behind and wait for their owner. When nobody comes to collect them or ask for them, they are unclaimed. «The lost property box is full of unclaimed coats.» The coats are still there because nobody has come to take them home.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. «Nobody has come for the parcel at the post office, so it is still waiting.» Waiting and nobody coming tell you that unclaimed means not collected or asked for by its owner.
explain: Unclaimed can also be used for land or money. «The old island was unclaimed, so no one owned it.» Try your meaning in the sentence: «The island was not collected or asked for by anyone» sounds odd, but «The island had no owner who asked for it» makes sense, so you can check the meaning that way.
fact: Unclaimed means not collected or asked for by the person it belongs to.
fact: «Unclaimed» is often used for lost property, prizes, parcels and bags.
fact: «The unclaimed prize sat on the desk all week.» The prize is waiting for its winner.
fact: In history, explorers sometimes wrongly called land «unclaimed», even when people already lived there and owned it.
fact: Phrases to know: «unclaimed prize», «unclaimed baggage», and «go unclaimed», which means nobody asks for it.
exercise: «The lost property box is full of unclaimed coats.» What does unclaimed mean here? | Bought by everyone in the class | Freshly washed and ready to wear | * Not collected by the people who own them | Hidden under the stairs
exercise: «Nobody has come for the parcel, so it is still unclaimed.» Why is the parcel unclaimed? | It has already been opened | It is too big to carry | * Nobody has come to collect it | It was sent to the wrong country
exercise: «The science fair prize went unclaimed all week.» What does went unclaimed suggest? | The prize was lost in the post | * Nobody asked for the prize | The prize was eaten by the class pet | The prize was given to two winners
test: «The unclaimed baggage went round and round the airport belt all day.» Find and copy one word that means the baggage was still waiting for its owner. | round | * unclaimed | airport | belt
test: Explorers called the land «unclaimed», but people already lived there. What does this show? | The explorers owned the land | The land had no people at all | * The explorers were wrong, because the land had owners | The land was empty and always had been
exam: Which sentence uses unclaimed correctly? | I unclaimed my lunch and then ate it quickly. | The unclaimed bus drove to the park every morning. | * Nobody has come for the lost umbrella, so it is still unclaimed. | The old umbrella sat by the door, and nobody has come for it, so it is unclaimed.
